      "doctor_question": "Hi, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, nice to meet you too. Um, I guess I came in because... well, I'm a high school teacher. And I'll sit down with a stack of essays or like, a new curriculum document, fully intending to just power through and work. \n\nLike, this past weekend I had this huge pile of papers on the Industrial Revolution. Which, honestly, the kids actually did a pretty good job on this year. Usually it's like pulling teeth to get 10th graders to care about the spinning jenny or textile mills, you know? One kid even made this little 3D model out of popsicle sticks for extra credit, which was wild because he usually never turns in his regular homework, so I was actually pretty impressed... \n\nBut, um, anyway, sorry. What was I saying? Right, the grading. I'll sit down to grade them, and within ten minutes I'll realize I’ve just been staring at the exact same page the whole time. Like, my eyes are on the paper, but I'm thinking about three completely different things—like if I need to get my car's oil changed, or a podcast I listened to yesterday—and I'm barely taking in a single word of what's actually in front of me.",
