      "doctor_question": "Did you have this kind of trouble focusing when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually, I did. I mean, even way back in primary school. I remember my parents used to get so frustrated with me. My mom had this whole filing system for my brother's schoolwork, like these color-coded binders, which is funny because my brother is an accountant now, so I guess the organization really rubbed off on him. He lives in Chicago, actually, just bought a place out there near the lake. \n\nBut anyway, my stuff? Not organized at all. My parents were constantly finding old worksheets just completely crumpled up at the bottom of my backpack. Like, I would actually do the homework sometimes and then just totally forget to turn it in. I had this blue JanSport bag that was basically a black hole for paper. And my report cards always said the exact same thing every single year. The teachers would write that I was bright but careless, or they would complain that I wouldn't finish my work unless I was being closely supervised by them. So yeah, it definitely goes pretty far back.",
